course: dictionary
lesson: 14867
title: Reactivity: how strongly things react
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Reactivity means how easily and how strongly something takes part in a change. In chemistry, it tells you how eagerly a substance joins in a chemical reaction. «Potassium has high reactivity.» So potassium joins in quickly and strongly.
explain: Some metals are very reactive and some hardly react at all. Scientists put metals in a reactivity series, from most reactive to least reactive. Potassium and sodium are at the top, and gold and platinum are at the bottom. «Gold has low reactivity, so it does not rust.»
explain: Reactivity can also describe people and bodies. In psychology, it means how strongly a person reacts to something, such as stress or an allergy trigger. «Her skin showed strong reactivity to the pollen» means her body reacted strongly to the pollen.
fact: Reactivity means how easily and how strongly something reacts.
fact: «High reactivity» means a substance reacts quickly and strongly.
fact: «Low reactivity» means a substance reacts slowly or hardly at all.
fact: The reactivity series puts metals from most reactive (potassium, sodium) to least reactive (gold, platinum).
fact: Sodium fizzes in water because it has high reactivity, and gold does not rust because it has low reactivity.
exercise: «Gold has low reactivity, so it does not rust.» What does low reactivity mean here? | It reacts very fast with everything | It is very heavy | It is a bright, shiny colour | *It does not easily take part in chemical reactions
exercise: «Sodium has high reactivity, so it fizzes in water.» What does high reactivity mean? | It is very cold to touch | It is very hard to melt | *It reacts strongly and quickly | It does not react at all
exercise: In the reactivity series, which metal is the most reactive? | *Potassium | Platinum | Copper | Gold
test: «Her skin showed strong reactivity to the pollen.» In this sentence, reactivity means: | The colour of her skin | How quickly she fell asleep | *How strongly her body reacted to the pollen | How much pollen she could carry
test: Which phrase describes a metal that rusts quickly in water? | *High reactivity | Reactivity is zero | Low reactivity | Reactivity series
exam: Which order goes from most reactive to least reactive? | *Potassium, sodium, gold | Sodium, gold, platinum | Gold, platinum, sodium | Gold, sodium, potassium
